1dod|n|Not paired with another, or remaining over after a pairing; without a mate; unmatched; single; as, an odd shoe; an odd glove. ; Not divisible by 2 without a remainder; not capable of being evenly paired, one unit with another; as, 1, 3, 7, 9, 11, etc., are odd numbers. ; Left over after a definite round number has been taken or mentioned; indefinitely, but not greatly, exceeding a specified number; extra. ; Remaining over; unconnected; detached; fragmentary; hence, occasional; inconsiderable; as, odd jobs; odd minutes; odd trifles. ; Different from what is usual or common; unusual; singular; peculiar; unique; strange.	a:16i4,7,4~16i4,7,4	v:1w9r,4,1~1w9r,4,1	V:1ijm,53,3;296o,29,1~1ijm,53,3;296o,29,1	n:1czl,9,3~1czl,9,3	N:1pqx,8,1;296i,1,1~1pqx,8,1;296i,1,1
1dod|a|Not paired with another, or remaining over after a pairing; without a mate; unmatched; single; as, an odd shoe; an odd glove. ; Not divisible by 2 without a remainder; not capable of being evenly paired, one unit with another; as, 1, 3, 7, 9, 11, etc., are odd numbers. ; Left over after a definite round number has been taken or mentioned; indefinitely, but not greatly, exceeding a specified number; extra. ; Remaining over; unconnected; detached; fragmentary; hence, occasional; inconsiderable; as, odd jobs; odd minutes; odd trifles. ; Different from what is usual or common; unusual; singular; peculiar; unique; strange.	j:1ijm,47,2;1d5e,41,10;6xw,41,8;efi,36,3;1d57,35,17;yko,33,14;1pr8,31,3;296o,29,1;1pqx,28,4;n3i,26,3~1d57,35,17;21y4,22,16;yko,33,14;1d5e,41,10;1v07,21,8;6xw,41,8;24cr,26,4;1pqx,28,4;13gh,9,4;n3i,26,3	e:lfo,74,3;qod,32,9;1vcq,31,7;1w24,26,6;1gns,18,3;1oar,11,14~1oar,11,14;qod,32,9;1vcq,31,7;1w24,26,6;lfo,74,3;1gns,18,3
1dof|n|The quality or state of being odd; singularity; queerness; peculiarity; as, oddity of dress, manners, and the like. ; That which is odd; as, a collection of oddities.	a:1dzo,38,2~1dzo,38,2
1doi|n|Difference in favor of one and against another; excess of one of two things or numbers over the other; inequality; advantage; superiority; hence, excess of chances; probability. ; Quarrel; dispute; debate; strife; -- chiefly in the phrase at odds.	a:vdr,25,6;16r0,21,1~vdr,25,6;16r0,21,1
